{"id": "section-body-17764", "title": "Angular cheilitis (angular stomatitis)", "chapterId": "chapter-sixteen", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "ORAL AND MAXILLOFACIAL CONDITIONS", "Fungal Infections", "Angular cheilitis (angular stomatitis)"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-17764", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Angular cheilitis (angular stomatitis)", "runs": [{"text": "Angular"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cheilitis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(angular"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "stomatitis)"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1126"}}, {"id": "body-17765", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Is a clinical entity characterized by erythema, rhagades, ulcerations, and crusting of one or both lip commissures and peri-labial skin, responsible of an unpleasant and painful discomfort.", "runs": [{"text": "Is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "entity"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "characterized"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "erythema,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rhagades,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ulcerations,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "crusting"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "one"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "both"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lip"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "commissures"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "peri-labial skin, responsible of an unpleasant and painful discomfort."}]}, {"id": "body-17766", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "The cause of Angular cheilitis is multifactorial and could range from local etiologies (Reduced or loss of vertical dimension of the jaws, Habitual lip licking or picking, Ill-fitting orthodontic appliances) to systemic ones (nutritional deficiencies, infection, chemicals).", "runs": [{"text": "The cause of Angular cheilitis is multifactorial and could range from local etiologies (Reduced or loss of vertical dimension of the jaws, Habitual lip licking or picking, Ill-fitting orthodontic appliances) to systemic ones (nutritional deficiencies, infection, chemicals)."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1100"}}, {"id": "body-17767", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentations", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentations"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-17768", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Angular cheilitis can be either unilateral or bilateral", "runs": [{"text": "Angular"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cheilitis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "can"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "either"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "unilateral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "bilateral"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1100"}}, {"id": "body-17769", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Soreness, erythema, pain, pruritus, burning sensation and fissuring at the angles of the mouth", "runs": [{"text": "Soreness,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "erythema,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pain,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pruritus,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "burning"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sensation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fissuring"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "at"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "angles"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mouth"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1100"}}, {"id": "body-17770", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Commonly associated with denture stomatitis s but may represent a nutritional deficiency or it may be related to orofacial granulomatosis or HIV infection", "runs": [{"text": "Commonly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "associated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "denture"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "stomatitis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "s"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "but"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "represent"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "nutritional"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "deficiency"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "it"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "related"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to orofacial granulomatosis or HIV infection"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1100"}}, {"id": "body-17772", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Non-Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Non-Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-17773", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Improve the vertical facial height by newer dentures or fillers", "runs": [{"text": "Improve"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "vertical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "facial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "height"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "newer"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dentures"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fillers"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1100"}}, {"id": "body-17774", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Habit cessation,", "runs": [{"text": "Habit"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cessation,"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1100"}}, {"id": "body-17775", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Proper fitting appliances", "runs": [{"text": "Proper"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fitting"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "appliances"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1100"}}, {"id": "body-17777", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-17778", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "When the condition is caused by fungal infection, the following topical formulas can be used", "runs": [{"text": "When"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "condition"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "caused"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fungal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infection,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "following"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "topical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "formulas"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "can"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "used"}]}, {"id": "body-17779", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A: nystatin suspension (PO) 100,000IU (1 ml) mixture held in the mouth for at least 3minutes before swallowing, 6hourly", "runs": [{"text": "A:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "nystatin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "suspension"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "100,000IU"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(1"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ml)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mixture"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "held"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mouth"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "at"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "least"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "3minutes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "before"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "swallowing,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "6hourly"}]}, {"id": "body-17780", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-17781", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "C: miconazole 2% oral gel apply 12 hourly for 7days", "runs": [{"text": "C:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "miconazole"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "2%"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "oral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "gel"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "apply"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "12"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hourly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "7days"}]}, {"id": "body-17783", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "When the condition is caused by bacteria, the following can be used", "runs": [{"text": "When"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "condition"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "caused"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "bacteria,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "following"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "can"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " used"}]}, {"id": "body-17784", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "C: lidocaine + chlorhexidine gluconate + metronidazole gel (PO) 8hourly at least for 7days", "runs": [{"text": "C:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "lidocaine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "+"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "chlorhexidine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "gluconate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "+"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "metronidazole"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "gel"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "8hourly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "at"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "least"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "7days"}]}, {"id": "body-17786", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Where topical application has failed, or candida infection has been considered severe; use.", "runs": [{"text": "Where"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "topical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "application"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "has"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "failed,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "candida"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infection"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "has"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "been"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "considered"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "severe;"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "use."}]}, {"id": "body-17787", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A: fluconazole (PO) 150mg 24hourly for 7days", "runs": [{"text": "A:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "fluconazole"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "150mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "24hourly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "7days"}]}, {"id": "body-17788", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-17789", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "D: itraconazole (PO) 200mg 24hourly for 7days", "runs": [{"text": "D:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "itraconazole"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "200mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "24hourly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "7days"}]}, {"id": "body-17790-textbox1-00001", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Note: Candidiasis has several risk factors; it is recommended that for HIV/AIDS patients with candidiasis, refer to the Tanzania HIV/AIDS Guidelines.", "runs": [{"text": "Note:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Candidiasis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "has"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "several"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "risk"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "factors;"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "it"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "recommended"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "that"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "HIV/AIDS"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patients"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "candidiasis,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "refer"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the Tanzania HIV/AIDS Guidelines."}]}, {"id": "body-17792", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Viral Infections", "runs": [{"text": "Viral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Infections"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1126"}}], "source": {"file": "medical.docx", "chapter": "Oral and maxillofacial conditions", "start": "body-17764", "end": "body-17792"}}